          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em persistence object
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            from a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+orders"} linear orders
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concept+with+an+attitude"} concept with an attitude
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+diagrams"} persistence diagrams
            or other measures of “persistence” as used in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+data+analysis"} topological data analysis
          %p
            The main example in this context arises when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+vector+spaces"} category of vector spaces
            or more generally a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+modules"} persistence modules
            as used in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistent+homology"} persistent homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            could be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+groups"} category of groups
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistent+homotopy"} persistent homotopy
          %p
            When the indexing poset is the poset of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            or, more generally, a product of copies of the poset of real numbers, the collection of persistent objects of a fixed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            admits a distance called the
            = succeed "," do
              %em interleaving distance
          %p
            The key property which one will typically demand of a good theory of persistence objects is a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+diagrams"} persistence diagrams
            (measuring “how persistent” a given persistence object is) which is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stability+of+persistence+diagrams"} stable
            with respect to interleaving distance.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            be a partially ordered set,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "partial+order#AsACategoryWithExtraProperties"} seen as a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a category. A
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              \-persistent object
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to C
            = succeed "-persistent" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^P
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R}, \leq)
            be the poset of real numbers with its standard order, and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a fixed category. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : \mathbb{R} \to C
            be a persistent object of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \geq 0 \in \mathbb{R}
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              \-shift
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the persistent object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X[\epsilon] : \mathbb{R} \to C
            such that, for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{R}
            we have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo +
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X[\epsilon](r) = X(r+\epsilon)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \leq s \in \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X[\epsilon](r) \to X[\epsilon](s)
            is equal to the structure morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo +
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo +
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(r+\epsilon) \to X(s+\epsilon)
            = succeed "-shift" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)[\epsilon] : C^\mathbb{R} \to C^\mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            give a natural transformation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^X_\epsilon : X \to X[\epsilon]
          %p
            An
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              \-interleaving
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            consists of natural transformations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y[\epsilon]
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : Y \to X[\epsilon]
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi η
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g[\epsilon] \circ f = \eta^X_{2\epsilon}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi ϵ
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f[\epsilon] \circ g = \eta^Y_{2\epsilon}
          %p
            As an example, note that a
            = succeed "-interleaving" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\mathbb{R}
          %p
            The
            %strong interleaving distance
            between persistent objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in C^{\mathbb{R}}
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi inf
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext and
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext are
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mtext -interleaved
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_I(X,Y) = inf\; \big(
                  \\big\{\epsilon \geq 0 \;:\;
                  X \;\text{and}\; Y\;\text{are}\; \epsilon\text{-interleaved}\;\big\}
                  \\cup \{ \infty \} \big).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R}, \leq)
            denote the poset of real numbers with its standard order, and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Vect
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect_k
            denote the category of vector spaces over a fixed field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-persistent" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Vect
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect_k
            are known as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+module"}
                %em persistence modules
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+data+analysis"} topological data analysis
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            be a natural number. Persistent objects of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Vect
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \to Vect_k
            are known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em multiparameter persistence modules
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
            denote the poset of non-negative real numbers with its standard order, and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            denote the category of sets. The
            = succeed "-persistent" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            are known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em persistent sets
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+module"} persistence module
          %h2#References References
          %p The terminology “persistence object” is used for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Pinckney"}> Donald Pinckney
              , Section 3.1
